# Next.js App Router

- Use the App Router in `frontend/app`. Do not introduce `pages/`.
- Default to Server Components. Add `"use client"` only for browser APIs, event handlers, or hooks.
- Import navigation from `next/navigation`, never `next/router`.
- In Next.js 16, `params` and `searchParams` are Promises. Await them in pages, layouts, and `generateMetadata`.
- Read current Next.js guidance in `frontend/node_modules/next/dist/docs/` and `frontend/AGENTS.md` before using APIs that may have changed.
- Place UI in `frontend/components/{map,analysis,zones,competitors}`.
- Shared helpers go in `frontend/lib`, hooks in `frontend/hooks`, shared types in `frontend/types`.
- Import with the `@/*` alias.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
import { useRouter } from "next/router";

// ✅ GOOD
import { useRouter } from "next/navigation";
```
